<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_PyrelandsIgniters_Comps.xml    PYRELANDS_MECHANICS_1 · 2026-09-11
  ============================================================================
  Attaches this mod's comps to the two igniter defs, which live in another mod
  (mandrake.rut.patches,
  src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/RUT_PyrelandsFauna.xml).

  🔑 WHY A PATCH AND NOT A NODE IN THE DEF ITSELF. A <li Class="..."> in a def
  is resolved against the loaded assemblies at def-parse time; writing these
  comps directly into RUT_PyrelandsFauna.xml would make that mod's defs depend
  on THIS mod's DLL and would break the moment the two are loaded apart. A
  patch from the later-loading mod has no such coupling: with this mod absent
  the igniters are simply ordinary animals again, which is exactly what they
  were before this item.

  Both operations are wrapped in PatchOperationFindMod so the file is a silent
  no-op rather than a wall of red if the igniter mod is not present.
  ⚠️ Remember that PatchOperationFindMod returns TRUE on no match — that is the
  point here (no-op, no error), but it means this file cannot report a missing
  def. If the comps appear to do nothing in game, check that the defs exist
  before suspecting the comps.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>RimUtinni Patches (Jawa campaign)</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <!-- ============================================================
             THE FIRE-HAWK (§7c). One comp, and it is only a marker plus a
             cooldown clock: the behaviour is the think-tree job-giver.
             🔴 Spread-only, never ex nihilo — the hawk cannot start a fire,
             only move one. That law lives in the job-giver's first gate;
             scanRadius here is how far it may look for a fire to steal from,
             NOT a chance to light one.
        ============================================================ -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_FireHawk"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <comps>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.PyrelandsMechanics.CompProperties_FireHawkSpread">
                <scanRadius>18</scanRadius>
                <spreadDistance>6</spreadDistance>
                <cooldownTicks>15000</cooldownTicks>
                <startFireSize>0.1</startFireSize>
              </li>
            </comps>
          </value>
        </li>

        <!-- ============================================================
             THE FURNACE-BEAST (§8b, §8c). Three comps, two of them the
             thermal circuit's two honest halves:

             1. CompProperties_HeatPusher — VANILLA. This is the enclosed-space
                half and it is free: a beast that wanders into a barn, a canyon
                room or a walled waystation genuinely heats it, because the
                vanilla temperature model spends pushed heat on the containing
                room. Calibrated against Campfire (MEASURED: heatPerSecond 21,
                heatPushMaxTemperature 28) — a little under a campfire, and it
                stops pushing once the room is comfortable.

             2. CompFurnaceWarmthAura — OURS. The open-field half, where a heat
                pusher does nothing a player can feel because outdoors the
                "room" is the whole map. A hediff aura instead: see
                Defs/HediffDefs/RUT_PyrelandsHediffs.xml.

             3. CompFurnaceBedIgnition — OURS. The bed-down smoulder.
                🔴 NO TAMED EXEMPTION, by ruling. Do not add one.
        ============================================================ -->
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="RUT_FurnaceBeast"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <comps>
              <li Class="CompProperties_HeatPusher">
                <heatPerSecond>18</heatPerSecond>
                <heatPushMaxTemperature>24</heatPushMaxTemperature>
              </li>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.PyrelandsMechanics.CompProperties_FurnaceWarmthAura">
                <radius>4.9</radius>
              </li>
              <li Class="RimMandrake.Utinni.PyrelandsMechanics.CompProperties_FurnaceBedIgnition" />
            </comps>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
